-- title:
--   Finiteness of the adelic class set at a congruence level
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be negative rational numbers and let $\mathbb H = \left(\frac{a,b}{\mathbb Q}\right)$ be the associated quaternion algebra, with finite-adelic points $\mathbb H \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$, the finite adele ring being that of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ in $\mathbb Q$. Let $\Lambda, P$ be $\mathbb Z$-submodules of $\mathbb H$ such that $\Lambda$ is an order in the sense of the project, namely $1 \in \Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb Q$-span of $\Lambda$ is all of $\mathbb H$, and $\Lambda$ is finitely generated; assume $P \le \Lambda$ and that for some nonzero natural number $n$ one has $n x \in P$ for every $x \in \Lambda$. For a $\mathbb Z$-submodule $M$, write $\widehat M$ for the additive subgroup of $\mathbb H \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ generated by the elements $z \otimes \alpha$ with $z \in M$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele integral at every height-one prime. Let $U$ be the subgroup of units $u$ of $\mathbb H \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ whose multiplication action stabilises both $\widehat\Lambda$ and $\widehat P$ setwise and satisfies $u x - x \in \widehat P$ for all $x \in \widehat \Lambda$. Then the double coset quotient of the unit group of $\mathbb H \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ by the image of $\mathbb H^\times$ under the diagonal embedding on the left and by $U$ on the right is a finite type.
--
--   This is Eichler's finiteness of the class number of an order in a definite rational quaternion algebra, in adelic form and at the congruence level attached to a pair $P \subseteq \Lambda$ with $n\Lambda \subseteq P$. It underlies the constructions in the Čerednik–Drinfeld tower, where Hecke correspondences and Eichler orders at a level are manipulated on a finite class set.
